summary: POST /query and the /query/* family — every operation over a set of metarecords takes a query.

|!Route |!Body |!Answers |
|`POST /repos/:repo/query` |`{"query", "select"?, "sort"?, "limit"?, "cursor"?, "count"?, "timeout_ms"?}` |the matches (below) |
|`POST /repos/:repo/query/delete` |`{"query"}` |`{"deleted": N}` |
|`POST /repos/:repo/query/fields/set` |`{"query", "name", "value" or "values", "force"?}` |`{"updated": N}` |
|`POST /repos/:repo/query/fields/add` |`{"query", "name", "value", "force"?}` |`{"updated": N}` |
|`POST /repos/:repo/query/fields/remove` |`{"query", "name", "value", "force"?}` |`{"updated": N}` |
|`POST /repos/:repo/query/fields/unset` |`{"query", "name", "force"?}` |`{"updated": N}` |
|`POST /repos/:repo/query/fields/resolve-tree` |`{"query", "field"?}` |`{"<uuid>": ["<path>"], …}` ([[Tree endpoints]]) |
|`POST /repos/:repo/query/profile` |a query |its phases ([[POST /repos/:repo/query/profile]]) |

!! POST /query

`select` shapes the items: absent, a list of uuids; a list of field names, metarecord
objects holding only those fields; `"*"`, whole metarecords. A field the metarecord
does not have is left out, not given as `nothing`:

```
[{"uuid": "…", "version": 8123456789,
  "fields": [{"id": 42, "name": "rating", "value": {"type": "int", "value": 5}}]}]
```

`sort`, `limit`, `cursor` and `count`: [[Pagination and sorting]]. `timeout_ms`:
[[Query limits]]. A query runs as an observable task; its errors are `400` for a
refused query, `409` for one stopped, `500` for a shape the evaluator cannot serve —
a daemon bug, never a slow answer ([[How queries are evaluated]]).

!! The set layer

Every operation over a ''set'' lives under `/query`, with a `query` in the body; a
`uuid_in` targets an explicit set (a multi-selection). Directly addressed things use
the resource routes ([[Metarecord endpoints]]); the two overlap only on one
metarecord, by design. A write over a set is ''one revision'', one operation per
metarecord changed ([[Editing metarecords from the command line]]); a reserved field
without `force` is a `400` ([[Reserved fields]]).

* ''delete'' removes every match, metadata and fields, atomically — no select-then-delete race. A set holding the repository root is refused whole ([[Referential integrity of a forest]]).
* ''set'' replaces every row of the name on each match; `values` sets several at once, repeated values collapsing to their first ([[No duplicate rows]]).
* ''add'' appends a row to each match; a match already holding the value is untouched, so `updated` counts the metarecords that gained a row and re-running it gives `0`.
* ''remove'' takes out the row equal to the value — at most one per match — leaving other rows and non-matches alone.
* ''unset'' removes every row of the name: the field becomes unknown, not `nothing`.
